# Development Workflow

## Quick Reference

```bash
make build                                                     # Build all crates
make test                                                      # Run all tests with one pinned embedded server
cargo run -p u-forge-ui-gpui                                   # Run the desktop app
```

> **No `source env.sh` required.** Bundled SQLite compiles with any standard C
> compiler on PATH. Lemonade Server on `localhost:13305` is auto-discovered.
> See [environment-config.mdc](mdc:.rulesdir/environment-config.mdc) for env
> vars and server setup.

---

## First Time Setup

1. Install Rust stable ([rustup.rs](https://rustup.rs)) and a C compiler
   (`gcc`, `clang`, or MSVC) — needed for `openssl-sys` (reqwest TLS).
2. `make build` — the first Ubuntu x64 build also downloads the pinned
   Embeddable Lemonade artifact. Set `UFORGE_SKIP_EMBEDDED_LEMONADE=1` to skip
   automatic provisioning; without an existing artifact the app stays
   graph-only.
3. Optionally install a standalone
   [Lemonade Server](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade) when developing
   against an externally managed service.
4. `make test` — provisions and owns one checksum-pinned embedded server for
   the complete suite, then tears down its process tree. No external server or
   environment configuration is required.
5. `cargo run -p u-forge-ui-gpui` — launch the desktop app.

